# GH issue #337: the team-performance evaluation harness (run_eval.py, via
# .github/workflows/eval.yml) generates and builds a REAL target product
# (a To-Do List Web App with real pip/npm dependencies - Flask, pytest-cov,
# etc.) inside the same network-isolated `agent` container #287 locked down
# to github.com/api.github.com only. check_build()'s `pip install -r
# requirements.txt`/`npm install` has no route to a package registry at all
# under that default allowlist, so every real dependency install fails
# outright - this is what a real eval run (0.1.0-run39) hit: a
# ModuleNotFoundError loop that no amount of retrying could ever fix,
# because the actual problem was the network layer, not the agent's code.
#
# This file is used ONLY by docker-compose.eval.yml, which ONLY the eval
# workflow's own `docker compose` invocations reference via an extra `-f`
# flag - real end-user projects (docker-compose.yaml/.local.yaml/
# .local-hostollama.yaml) are completely untouched by this file and keep
# the default, narrower allowlist.filter. Per the issue's own decision,
# this is a checked-in file requiring a normal human-reviewed PR to change
# - there is no runtime/agent-driven mechanism that can broaden it.
#
# Same matching rules as allowlist.filter: one regex per line, matched
# against the CONNECT (HTTPS) target host[:port].
^github\.com(:[0-9]+)?$
^api\.github\.com(:[0-9]+)?$
# PyPI - pip's index lookup and the actual package-file download host
# (package files are served from files.pythonhosted.org, not pypi.org
# itself).
^pypi\.org(:[0-9]+)?$
^files\.pythonhosted\.org(:[0-9]+)?$
# npm's package registry.
^registry\.npmjs\.org(:[0-9]+)?$
